# The periodic Dolbeault equation on the actual period cover

This family constructs a smooth periodic primitive of every smooth closed
`(0,1)` form after subtracting its actual Haar-mean components. The Fourier
coefficients, their inverse-symbol bounds, convergence, all-order smoothness,
coefficient recovery, and the passage through the genuine period lattice
are all proved in the imported files.
